      "text": "Let's denote the complex number \\(\\alpha\\) as \\(\\alpha = a + bi\\) where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are real numbers. The conjugate of \\(\\alpha\\) is \\(\\beta = a - bi\\) and its complex conjugate is \\(\\overline{\\beta} = a + bi\\). The condition that \\(\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta^2}\\) is real implies:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta^2} = \\frac{a + bi}{(a - bi)^2} \n\\]\n\nFirst, simplify \\(\\beta^2\\):\n\n\\[\n\\beta^2 = (a - bi)^2 = a^2 + 2abi - b^2\n\\]\n\nNow form \\(\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta^2}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta^2} = \\frac{a + bi}{a^2 + 2abi - b^2}\n\\]\n\nTo clear the denominator, multiply the numerator and the denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a + bi}{a^2 + 2abi - b^2} \\cdot \\frac{a^2 - 2abi - b^2}{a^2 - 2abi - b^2} = \\frac{(a + bi)(a^2 - 2abi - b^2)}{(a^2 + 2abi - b^2)(a^2 - 2abi - b^2)}\n\\]\n\nThe denominator simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\n(a^2 + 2abi - b^2)^2 = a^4 - 4a^2b^2 + (2abi)^2 = a^4 - 4a^2b^2 - 4ab^2i^2\n\\]\n\nThe numerator simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n(a + bi)(a^2 - 2abi - b^2) = a(a^2 - 2abi - b^2) + (bi)(a^2 - 2abi - b^2)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying \\(a(a^2 + 2abi) + bi(a^2 + 2abi) - abi^2 - b^2bi\\) we see only:\n\n\\[\nai(a^2 + 2abi) + bi(a^2 + 2abi) + (-abi^2 - b^2bi) = 2abi(a^2 - b^2)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\beta^2 = (a^2 + b^2)(a^2 - b^2) = a^4 - b^4\n\\]\n\nHence,\n\n\\[\n|\\alpha - \\beta| = |\\alpha + \\beta| \\Rightarrow \\mid 1 - 2abi \\mid = 2 \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, \n\n\\[\n|1 - 2abi|^2 = (1 - 2abi)(1 + 2abi) = 1 + 4a^2b^2 = (2\\sqrt{3}) \\Rightarrow 1 + 4a^2b^2 = 12\n\\]\n\nFrom this we solve for \\(4a^2b^2 = 11\\):\n\n\\[\na^2b^2 = \\frac{11}{4}\n\\]\n\nNow we use the derived determinant to solve for the real number \\(a^2 + b^2\\) and the magnitude of \\(\\alpha\\):\n\nUsing \\( |\\alpha| = |a+ib| \\):\n\nThus\n\n\\[\na^2 + b^2 = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} \\Rightarrow (a^2 + b^2)^2 = 11 \\implies a^2 + b^2 = \\sqrt{11}\n\\]\n\nHence, \n\n\\[\n|\\alpha| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2} = \\sqrt{11}\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{11}}\\)",
